rename_choice.description:
Home Assistant renamed {old} to {new}. Tag Historian goes on storing its readings in the tag {old_tag} meanwhile, so the history goes on and nothing is lost.{refusal}

Rename the tag, and its whole history - the readings from before included - reads as {new_tag} from now on, and new readings are stored under that name. Nothing is copied: it is the same history under a new name, and it can be renamed back in the Tag Historian dashboard.

Or start a new tag, {new_tag}, for the readings from now on, and leave the history where it is, under {old_tag}. That takes one more tag on your plan.

merge_choice.description:
Home Assistant renamed {old} to {new}, a name that has a tag in Tag Historian already: {new_tag}. The renamed entity's history from before the rename is in {old_tag}, and its readings go on into {old_tag} until you choose, so nothing is lost.{refusal}

Merge them, and the two read as one history under {new_tag}, and new readings are stored there. Where both have readings in the same hour, that hour's figures are worked out from both, and {old_tag} stops counting as a tag. Nothing is copied, and the merge can be undone in the Tag Historian dashboard.

Or keep them apart: {old_tag} keeps its history as a tag of its own, and the readings from now on go into {new_tag}.
